摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"DeepSeek WebUI Studio for interactive, visual-first client plugin development","id":"gh:1335758340","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-webui-studio","slug":"memorax-ai/dsh-webui-studio","topics":["deepseek","deepseek-harness","developer-tools","dsh","dsh-plugin","harmony","local-development","plugin-development","react","typescript","visual-editor","vite","webui"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"DeepSeek WebUI Studio for interactive, visual-first client plugin development"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"DeepSeek WebUI Studio"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"A visual-first studio for building DSH WebUI plugins."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Inspect the real interface, edit source, run builds, and validate patches without loading unfinished"},{"id":"p4s2","text":" code into your stable DSH Host."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"Powered by dsh-harmony."},{"id":"p6s1","text":"Get started"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"Report a bug"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Request a feature"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"简体中文 / English"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## What you can do"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"- [x] Create a minimal DSH Web Client plugin or import an existing local plugin folder\n- [x] Give ev"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"ery Draft its own Git worktree, `DSH_HOME`, profile, dependencies, and child Host\n- [x] Preview the "},{"id":"p11s3","text":"official WebUI without loading Draft code into the stable Host\n- [x] Browse normally or inspect DOM,"},{"id":"p11s4","text":" React owners, source candidates, and Patch traces\n- [x] Surface plugin-registered Element controls "},{"id":"p11s5","text":"automatically; save defaults and subtree-scoped CSS back to Draft source\n- [x] Review Component decl"},{"id":"p11s6","text":"aration matches and generate CSS decorators without changing existing call-site props\n- [x] Reorder "},{"id":"p11s7","text":"and toggle both Harmony providers and individual Patches through one transactional reload\n- [x] Edit"},{"id":"p11s8","text":" Draft source with CodeMirror and protect installed dependency sources as read-only\n- [x] Build, app"},{"id":"p11s9","text":"ly through Harmony, reload, and confirm the live Client graph revision\n- [x] Start a Draft-scoped Ag"},{"id":"p11s10","text":"ent or continue an existing DSH session with temporary Studio tools, skill, and context\n- [x] Let an"},{"id":"p11s11","text":" external Agent inspect the running WebUI through a local read-only Streamable HTTP MCP endpoint\n- ["},{"id":"p11s12","text":"x] Answer one-shot tool approvals, structured questions, and plan reviews without leaving Studio\n- ["},{"id":"p11s13","text":"x] Check package exports, artifacts, Patch state, ordering, dependencies, and pack output\n- [x] Run "},{"id":"p11s14","text":"multiple isolated Draft Preview Hosts at the same time\n- [x] Snapshot the current WebUI profile or a"},{"id":"p11s15","text":"nother local profile into each isolated Draft runtime\n- [x] Reorder plugins and enable or disable Ha"},{"id":"p11s16","text":"rmony Providers through one transactional hot reload"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"## How it works"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"The stable Host owns the Studio interface, Draft registry, and Agent sessions.\nEach Draft owns an is"},{"id":"p14s2","text":"olated worktree and child Preview Host. A build becomes\nactive only after the Preview confirms the n"},{"id":"p14s3","text":"ew live Client graph revision.\nStopping a Draft terminates its child Host but preserves its files an"},{"id":"p14s4","text":"d state.\nAn existing ordinary DSH session can enter Studio mode without losing its\nhistory or identi"},{"id":"p14s5","text":"ty. Leaving Studio removes the scoped Draft tools, skill, and\ncontext so the session resumes through"},{"id":"p14s6","text":" its ordinary DSH composition."},{"id":"p15s1","text":"Studio is served locally at:"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"External Agents can connect to the running instance through MCP at:"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"A typical MCP client entry is:"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Add that URL as a Streamable HTTP MCP server in the external Agent. It exposes\n`studio_get_context`,"},{"id":"p21s2","text":" `studio_get_selection`, `studio_get_harmony_profile`,\n`studio_inspect_harmony_target`, `studio_read"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"_dependency_source`, and\n`studio_preview_status`. These tools inspect the current Host only; the ext"},{"id":"p21s4","text":"ernal\nAgent remains responsible for editing and building its own WebUI project. Harmony\nprofile, Pat"},{"id":"p21s5","text":"ch, and dependency-source inspection work directly from the Host.\nDOM selection is available while S"},{"id":"p21s6","text":"tudio is open and an element is selected in\nthe current-instance Preview. The endpoint follows Studi"},{"id":"p21s7","text":"o's existing loopback-only\nboundary, including access through an SSH loopback tunnel."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"Its managed data lives under `$DSH_HOME/studio/`:"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"Creating a new plugin initializes and commits a minimal DSH Web Client package.\nNew plugins stay ins"},{"id":"p24s2","text":"ide Studio by default. Creation can optionally record an\nabsolute destination for a new or empty loc"},{"id":"p24s3","text":"al folder; Studio does not create\nor modify that folder until **Save plugin to folder** is used from"},{"id":"p24s4","text":" the instance\npanel. Later saves synchronize the Studio-owned project snapshot while leaving\ndestina"},{"id":"p24s5","text":"tion-only files such as `node_modules` untouched.\nImporting an existing plugin accepts an absolute l"},{"id":"p24s6","text":"ocal folder after validating\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"### Why not simply ask an Agent to edit the source?"},{"id":"p26s1","text":"Studio still connects to the real Agent inside DSH. It gives that Agent richer\nproject context, inte"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"grated previews, purpose-built tools and skills, and a\ntighter edit-build-inspect-validate loop. Stu"},{"id":"p26s3","text":"dio does not replace the Agent; it\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"## Compatibility work in progress"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"The development dependencies use one coordinated DSH 0.1.5-rc.3 release, with\nthe matching npm lockf"},{"id":"p28s2","text":"ile. Dependabot groups the DSH development packages so\ntheir peer requirements are updated together."},{"id":"p28s3","text":" CI also retains the isolated\n0.1.5-rc.2 compatibility baseline and checks 0.1.5-rc.3 explicitly."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"The development baseline pins Cordis 4.0.2, its loader 1.0.3, and group 1.0.2\nto match DSH's peer re"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"quirements. Dependabot skips newer versions of these\npackages: DSH requires this Cordis/group pair, "},{"id":"p29s3","text":"and newer loaders require newer\nCordis. Reassess the pins and exclusions when updating the coordinat"},{"id":"p29s4","text":"ed DSH\ndevelopment release. Cordis 4.0.4 and loader 1.0.5 also fail npm peer resolution\nwhen upgrade"},{"id":"p29s5","text":"lopment release. Cordis 4.0.4 and loader 1.0.5 also fail npm peer resolution\nwhen upgraded together."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"This branch targets DSH 0.1.5-rc.2 through 0.1.7-rc.2 and the 0.2.0-rc.1 prerelease with the native "},{"id":"p30s2","text":"Session Controller and Binding Gateway events. Isolated 0.1.7-rc.2 and 0.2.0-rc.1 checks cover Studi"},{"id":"p30s3","text":"o HTTP serving, RPC, session snapshot, control, journal, history, model APIs, and the full Draft Pre"},{"id":"p30s4","text":"view lifecycle. They do not cover browser interaction."},{"id":"p31s1","text":"The adapter follows per-Session journals and assistant streams, reconstructs the active prefix after"},{"id":"p31s2","text":" reconnecting, and returns native approval/question results. Preview Hosts retain the authenticated "},{"id":"p31s3","text":"launch URL and use an exchanged cookie for their backend connection. The Harmony installer startup f"},{"id":"p31s4","text":"ix must also ship before validating fresh installations."},{"id":"p32s1","text":"`npm run test:gateway -- <upstream-install-root> <harmony-lib/bin.js>` exercises Studio RPC, Session"},{"id":"p32s2","text":" snapshots, projections, history, model catalog and journal delivery against an isolated real Host. "},{"id":"p32s3","text":"The Windows rc package/Preview integration test also passes. Browser interaction and cross-platform "},{"id":"p32s4","text":"checks remain separate release gates."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
